<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thomas Clarkson</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1760">1760</a>–<a href="/years/1846">1846</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Thomas Clarkson was an English campaigner against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">slave trade</a>. After winning a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambridge">Cambridge</a> essay prize on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> in 1785, he helped found the Society for Effecting the Abolition of the Slave Trade in 1787 and travelled widely gathering evidence from sailors and ports. His research supplied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-wilberforce">William Wilberforce</a>'s campaign in Parliament, which achieved abolition of the British slave trade in 1807.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thomas-clarkson.jpg" alt="Thomas Clarkson" width="320" height="416" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Carl Frederik von Breda · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Thomas_Clarkson_by_Carl_Frederik_von_Breda.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
